BT /F1 9.6 Tf 62.0 705.8 Td (- sandbox.allowUnsandboxedCommands: false - blocks any command that the sandbox can't enforce) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 50.0 693.2 Td (  against \(e.g. binaries that escape the OS-level isolation\). The default is permissive on some) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 50.0 680.6 Td (  platforms; banking-grade deployments should explicitly set this false.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 62.0 668.0 Td (- denyRead covers .env, AWS / SSH credential dirs, and ./secrets/* at the OS level. Unlike) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 50.0 655.4 Td (  permission rules, this can't be bypassed by a subprocess opening the file directly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 62.0 642.8 Td (- denyWrite keeps the agent out of the home directory \(outside the project\), /etc \(system) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 50.0 630.2 Td (  config\), and /usr \(system binaries\). The sandbox already denies write to the filesystem root) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 50.0 617.6 Td (  by default, so listing / is redundant; we list ~/** explicitly because the home directory is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 50.0 605.0 Td (  otherwise a common write target.) Tj ET
